],"type":"Other literature type","urls":["https://dx.doi.org/10.25220/wnj.v04.i1.0002"],"refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"openaire____::55045bd2a65019fd8e6741a755395c8c","value":"Unknown Repository"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::5f532a3fc4f1ea403f37070f59a7a53a","value":"Microsoft Academic Graph"}}],"links":[],"otherTitles":null,"inDiamondJournal":false,"green":false,"isGreen":false,"isInDiamondJournal":false},{"authors":[{"id":"orcid_______::b2e95c434d802db6e04baa7e86c8cc56","fullName":"Elena Tanase","name":"Elena","surname":"Tanase","rank":1,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0009-0006-1627-2563"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Larisa Mihaela Marusca","name":"Larisa Mihaela","surname":"Marusca","rank":2,"pid":null},{"id":"orcid_______::c08036e91e885f6dc9c984271a4516e1","fullName":"Florin George Horhat","name":"Florin George","surname":"Horhat","rank":3,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0001-6133-0204"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Monica Susan","name":"Monica","surname":"Susan","rank":4,"pid":null},{"id":"orcid_______::0e3478454e3c708dc0a1f9e5172f2f15","fullName":"Razvan Susan","name":"Razvan","surname":"Susan","rank":5,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0003-3531-3974"},"provenance":null}},{"id":"orcid_______::8e388024caa17624b1c1e07753c024bd","fullName":"Razvan Horhat","name":"Razvan","surname":"Horhat","rank":6,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0003-1836-6927"},"provenance":null}},{"id":"orcid_______::445be893752014733eba57584f81efbb","fullName":"Stefania Dinu","name":"Stefania","surname":"Dinu","rank":7,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0002-4351-7726"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Tiberiu-Liviu Dragomir","name":"Tiberiu-Liviu","surname":"Dragomir","rank":8,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Sonia Tanasescu","name":"Sonia","surname":"Tanasescu","rank":9,"pid":null}],"openAccessColor":"gold","publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"eng","label":"English"},"countries":null,"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0301 basic medicine"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Male"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0303 health sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Adolescent"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Romania"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Incidence"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Infant"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"vitamin D"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Vitamin D Deficiency"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Article"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"03 medical and health sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"respiratory infections"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"food supplements"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Cross-Sectional Studies"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Child, Preschool"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Dietary Supplements"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Humans"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Female"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Vitamin D"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Child"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Respiratory Tract Infections"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"Assessing the Impact of Vitamin D Supplementation on Respiratory Infections in Children and Adolescents: A Cross-Sectional Study","subTitle":null,"descriptions":["<jats:p>Background and Objectives: Recent studies suggest that vitamin D supplementation and higher serum 25-hydroxyvitamin D (25-OHD) concentrations may reduce the incidence of respiratory infections in children and adolescents. This cross-sectional study aimed to evaluate the association between different concentrations of vitamin D supplementation, serum 25-OHD concentrations, and the frequency of respiratory infections among individuals aged 1 to 18 years, for a duration of 2 years. Methods: Concerning sun exposure in relation to vitamin D, the study took place in Romania, at approximately 45-degree northern latitude. A total of 194 patients were divided into groups based on weekly vitamin D supplementation (&lt;400 IU, 400–800 IU, &gt;800 IU), serum 25-OHD concentrations (&lt;20 ng/mL, 20–30 ng/mL, &gt;30 ng/mL), and age (&lt;6 years, 6–12 years, 12–18 years). The overall incidence of respiratory infections was 41.2%. Results: Participants receiving &gt;800 IU/week had a significantly lower incidence of infections (16.7%) compared to those receiving &lt;400 IU/week (60.0%, p &lt; 0.001). Similarly, participants with serum 25-OHD concentrations &gt;30 ng/mL had an infection rate of 16.7%, compared to 61.4% in those with concentrations &lt;20 ng/mL (p &lt; 0.001). Age-specific analyses revealed that the protective effect of vitamin D was most pronounced in children under 6 years old. Logistic regression showed that higher vitamin D supplementation and serum 25-OHD concentrations were independently associated with reduced odds of respiratory infections (OR = 0.25 and OR = 0.22, respectively, p &lt; 0.001). Conclusions: These findings support the potential role of vitamin D supplementation in preventing respiratory infections in the pediatric population.</jats:p>"],"publicationDate":"2024-11-19","publisher":"MDPI AG","embargoEndDate":null,"sources":["Crossref","Nutrients","Volume 16","Issue 22","Pages: 3953"],"formats":["application/pdf"],"contributors":null,"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/"},"container":{"name":"Nutrients","issnPrinted":null,"issnOnline":"2072-6643","issnLinking":null,"ep":null,"iss":null,"sp":"3953","vol":"16","edition":null,"conferencePlace":null,"conferenceDate":null},"documentationUrls":null,"codeRepositoryUrl":null,"programmingLanguage":null,"contactPeople":null,"contactGroups":null,"tools":null,"size":null,"version":null,"geoLocations":null,"id":"doi_dedup___::bacdd206f6317c0f0a6212f0b018c6a7","originalIds":["nu16223953","10.3390/nu16223953","50|doiboost____|bacdd206f6317c0f0a6212f0b018c6a7","od_______267::d27e0399f9a9fa6643638a20ceafc3ac","39599738","PMC11597694","oai:pubmedcentral.nih.gov:11597694","50|od_______267::d27e0399f9a9fa6643638a20ceafc3ac","50|multidiscipl::4ba7caa8bf07a2ced75f1d8ebf56fb36","oai:mdpi.com:/2072-6643/16/22/3953/"],"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.3390/nu16223953"},{"scheme":"pmid","value":"39599738"},{"scheme":"pmc","value":"PMC11597694"}],"dateOfCollection":null,"lastUpdateTimeStamp":null,"indicators":{"citationImpact":{"citationCount":7.0,"influence":2.297249E-9,"popularity":6.406967E-9,"impulse":7.0,"citationClass":"C5","influenceClass":"C5","impulseClass":"C4","popularityClass":"C4"}},"projects":null,"organizations":[{"legalName":"Department of Pediatrics","acronym":"Department of Pediatrics","id":"pending_org_::0acceafcaa75299638bc0a7abbb1353c","pids":null,"countries":[{"code":"IL","label":"Israel"}],"websiteurl":null},{"legalName":"Victor Babeș University of Medicine and Pharmacy Timișoara","acronym":"UMFT","id":"openorgs____::3cdea2290f12a259eb6e52581cfca837","pids":[{"scheme":"OrgReg","value":"RO0040"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q851648"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"0000000105044027"},{"scheme":"PIC","value":"997902051"},{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.22248.3e"},{"scheme":"OrgRef","value":"1598766"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q851648"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/00afdp487"}],"countries":[{"code":"RO","label":"Romania"}],"websiteurl":"http://www.umft.ro/"}],"communities":null,"collectedFrom":[{"key":"openaire____::c2cdfa5866e03cdd07d313cbc8fb8311","value":"Multidisciplinary Digital Publishing Institute"},{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"},{"key":"opendoar____::8b6dd7db9af49e67306feb59a8bdc52c","value":"Europe PubMed Central"},{"key":"opendoar____::eda80a3d5b344bc40f3bc04f65b7a357","value":"PubMed Central"}],"instances":[{"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.3390/nu16223953"}],"license":"CC BY","accessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/","openAccessRoute":"gold"},"type":"Article","urls":["https://doi.org/10.3390/nu16223953"],"publicationDate":"2024-11-19","refereed":"peerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"doajarticles::253e0792781052f6209709122ab03589","value":"Nutrients"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"}},{"pids":[{"scheme":"pmid","value":"39599738"},{"scheme":"pmc","value":"PMC11597694"}],"alternateIdentifiers":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.3390/nu16223953"}],"accessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/","openAccessRoute":"gold"},"type":"Article","urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39599738"],"publicationDate":"2024-11-27","refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"doajarticles::253e0792781052f6209709122ab03589","value":"Nutrients"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"opendoar____::8b6dd7db9af49e67306feb59a8bdc52c","value":"Europe PubMed Central"}},{"alternateIdentifiers":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.3390/nu16223953"}],"license":"CC BY","accessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/","openAccessRoute":null},"type":"Article","urls":["http://dx.doi.org/10.3390/nu16223953"],"publicationDate":"2024-11-19","refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"opendoar____::eda80a3d5b344bc40f3bc04f65b7a357","value":"PubMed Central"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"opendoar____::eda80a3d5b344bc40f3bc04f65b7a357","value":"PubMed Central"}},{"alternateIdentifiers":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.3390/nu16223953"}],"license":"CC BY","accessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/","openAccessRoute":"gold"},"type":"Article","urls":["https://dx.doi.org/10.3390/nu16223953"],"publicationDate":"2024-11-19","refereed":"peerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"doajarticles::253e0792781052f6209709122ab03589","value":"Nutrients"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::c2cdfa5866e03cdd07d313cbc8fb8311","value":"Multidisciplinary Digital Publishing Institute"}}],"links":[],"otherTitles":null,"inDiamondJournal":false,"green":true,"isGreen":true,"isInDiamondJournal":false},{"authors":[{"id":"orcid_______::44528c4dfd84af811e08d438b1c3b0df","fullName":"Oana Silvana Sarau","name":"Oana Silvana","surname":"Sarau","rank":1,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0009-0000-0927-9544"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Hari Charan Rachabattuni","name":"Hari Charan","surname":"Rachabattuni","rank":2,"pid":null},{"id":"orcid_______::998ba65fccb12c047d439fbacd1704c4","fullName":"Sai Teja Gadde","name":"Sai Teja","surname":"Gadde","rank":3,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0009-0007-7800-7666"},"provenance":null}},{"id":"orcid_______::bd504de65ce24465528b724f41144019","fullName":"Sai Praveen Daruvuri","name":"Sai Praveen","surname":"Daruvuri","rank":4,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0009-0007-6789-583x"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Larisa Mihaela Marusca","name":"Larisa Mihaela","surname":"Marusca","rank":5,"pid":null},{"id":"orcid_______::c08036e91e885f6dc9c984271a4516e1","fullName":"Florin George Horhat","name":"Florin George","surname":"Horhat","rank":6,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0001-6133-0204"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Ariadna Petronela Fildan","name":"Ariadna Petronela","surname":"Fildan","rank":7,"pid":null},{"id":"orcid_______::b2e95c434d802db6e04baa7e86c8cc56","fullName":"Elena Tanase","name":"Elena","surname":"Tanase","rank":8,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0009-0006-1627-2563"},"provenance":null}},{"id":"orcid_______::9e6e0a70e25e4277dc7682347a48aced","fullName":"Catalin Prodan-Barbulescu","name":"Catalin","surname":"Prodan-Barbulescu","rank":9,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0003-4348-5469"},"provenance":null}},{"id":"orcid_______::d3b6929fedb1bf4bc33e6726095e2698","fullName":"Delia Ioana Horhat","name":"Delia Ioana","surname":"Horhat","rank":10,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0001-7210-1263"},"provenance":null}}],"openAccessColor":"gold","publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"eng","label":"English"},"countries":null,"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0301 basic medicine"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Male"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Romania"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Incidence"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Infant"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"vitamin D"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Vitamin D Deficiency"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Article"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"SDG","value":"3. Good health"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"03 medical and health sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"respiratory infections"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0302 clinical medicine"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Cross-Sectional Studies"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"children"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Recurrence"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Child, Preschool"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Dietary Supplements"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Humans"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Female"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"blood tests"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Vitamin D"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Respiratory Tract Infections"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"Exploring the Preventive Potential of Vitamin D against Respiratory Infections in Preschool-Age Children: A Cross-Sectional Study","subTitle":null,"descriptions":["<jats:p>Recent studies hypothesized that vitamin D supplementation and subsequent higher 25(OH)D serum levels could protect against respiratory infections in children. This cross-sectional study, conducted from May 2022 to December 2023 in Timisoara, Romania, aimed to evaluate the potential influence of vitamin D supplementation on the incidence of respiratory infections among preschool-age children. This study examined 215 children over 18 months who were split into a group of patients with recurrent respiratory infections (n = 141) and another group of patients with only one respiratory tract infection in the past 12 months (n = 74). Patients were evaluated based on their serum vitamin D levels 25(OH)D, demographic characteristics, and health outcomes. The study identified that preschool-age children with recurrent infections had significantly lower mean vitamin D concentrations (24.5 ng/mL) compared to the control group (29.7 ng/mL, p &lt; 0.001). Additionally, a higher proportion of vitamin D deficiency was observed among children with recurrent infections in the past 12 months. Notably, vitamin D supplementation above 600 IU/week significantly reduced the likelihood of respiratory infections, evidenced by an odds ratio of 0.523 (p &lt; 0.001), indicating that preschool-age children receiving a dose of vitamin D higher than 600 IU/week were about half as likely to experience respiratory infections compared to those who did not. Furthermore, no significant associations were found between sun exposure, daily sunscreen use, and the incidence of respiratory infections. Conclusively, this study underscores the potential role of vitamin D in helping the immune system against respiratory infections in preschool-age children. The observed protective effect of vitamin D supplementation suggests a potential public health strategy to mitigate the incidence of respiratory infections in preschool children on top of the already known benefits.</jats:p>"],"publicationDate":"2024-05-23","publisher":"MDPI AG","embargoEndDate":null,"sources":["Crossref","Nutrients","Volume 16","Issue 11","Pages: 1595"],"formats":["application/pdf"],"contributors":null,"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/"},"container":{"name":"Nutrients","issnPrinted":null,"issnOnline":"2072-6643","issnLinking":null,"ep":null,"iss":null,"sp":"1595","vol":"16","edition":null,"conferencePlace":null,"conferenceDate":null},"documentationUrls":null,"codeRepositoryUrl":null,"programmingLanguage":null,"contactPeople":null,"contactGroups":null,"tools":null,"size":null,"version":null,"geoLocations":null,"id":"doi_dedup___::85f2454b53f5d4479f7a27510de7b161","originalIds":["nu16111595","10.3390/nu16111595","50|doiboost____|85f2454b53f5d4479f7a27510de7b161","od_______267::16f82069578401e3bda9d9be5e0d5b8a","38892528","PMC11173803","50|od_______267::16f82069578401e3bda9d9be5e0d5b8a","oai:pubmedcentral.nih.gov:11173803","50|multidiscipl::787c217f814f66569e12510c01e476f2","oai:mdpi.com:/2072-6643/16/11/1595/"],"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.3390/nu16111595"},{"scheme":"pmid","value":"38892528"},{"scheme":"pmc","value":"PMC11173803"}],"dateOfCollection":null,"lastUpdateTimeStamp":null,"indicators":{"citationImpact":{"citatio